# Git Commits — Clean Messages Only

Never add ticket placeholders, tool attribution, or vendor trailers to commit messages.

## Forbidden in commit subject or body

- **CN-* prefixes** — e.g. `CN-0011:`, `CN-XXXX:`, or any `CN-` ticket placeholder
- **Cursor attribution** — e.g. `Co-authored-by: Cursor <cursoragent@cursor.com>`
- **Other tool footers** — e.g. `Made-with: Cursor`, `Made with Cursor`

## Required format

Use conventional commits only — subject (+ optional body) with no extra trailers:

```
feat: add mistral.rs HTTP backend

Optional body paragraph explaining why.
```

## When committing via git

- Use only the subject and body the user requested
- Do not append CN-* placeholders “for AI-generated commits”
- Do not append Co-authored-by or Made-with lines from the IDE or agent
